# No "craft" language

Do not use the word **craft** (or **Craft**) anywhere in user-facing copy — headings, body text, blog tags, metadata, CTAs, docs, or marketing.

## Use instead

| Instead of | Prefer |
|---|---|
| craft / craftsmanship | judgment, standards, taste, care, attention, execution |
| crafted | built, designed, made, refined |
| craft-led | detail-led, standards-led |

## Examples

```
❌ "A studio that cares about craft"
✅ "A studio that cares about the details"

❌ tag: Craft
✅ tag: Details

❌ "Craft and engineering"
✅ "Design and engineering"
```

When reviewing or writing copy, scan for `craft` case-insensitively and replace before shipping.
